~ start
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=true
do GameDialogueManager.show_character("Mysterious Person")
Mysterious Person : Goodness! You're finally awake. Time to stop these vermin from reaching the server!
| Mysterious Person : I thought I had lost you!
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=false
Player: Wait, who are you?
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=true
do GameDialogueManager.show_character("Mysterious Person")
Mysterious Person: Right..
Mysterious Person: I forgot to introduce myself.  My name is Odysseus. I will be your Guide!
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=false
Odysseus: I have been protecting the SERVER for so long. Thankfully, you are here now! 
Player: What? Wait, where are we?
Odysseus: Save the chatter for later! See those? Ohh, Spams! They come unwelcome, unsolicited, and in large quantities. So be ready!
do get_tree().create_timer(1.0).timeout
Odysseus: Can you see the server's health? It helps you visualize how many beatings it takes before the SERVER collapses. You don’t want to let it drop to 0! 
Player: These things are so annoying.
Guide: Spam incoming, get ready.
=> END

~ spam_filter
Odysseus: Good choice! That tower is called Spam Filter; this was specifically built for this cyber threat.  They have automated security tools that identify, block, redirect, or allow bulk, unwanted, or malicious emails.
Player: Since when do cyberthreats turn into monsters? 
Odysseus: I'll explain later. 
Odysseus: Now, each enemy drops money and exp points for you to upgrade your towers. Let's ramp up its damage before we get overtaken by them.
Odysseus: Each tower upgrade is important to make your offense stronger. By maxing the upgrades from the first tier, you can unlock upgrades of a stronger caliber.
=> END

~ spam_defeat
Odysseus: That was close!
Player: Upgrading the canon saves us from that cliff. It really does keep these threats at bay!
Odysseus: Now, don't be hasty; there are many cyber threats out there that you have not encountered yet. Each of them has ways to find weaknesses in your defense and evolve to find an exploit in your system. This does not mean that these threats will stay the same as you encounter them.
Player: It's about time that you do the explaining on what on earth is happening!

=> END

~ backstory
Player: Why am I not able to remember anything? The last thing I remember was waking up from a headache.
Odysseus: That is not unusual. A lot of people suffer from different side effects of the artificial magnetic field generated by 10 interconnected S.E.R.V.E.R across the globe.  
Player: Did you say 10?
Odysseus: Yes, to mimic the natural magnetic field of Earth. Normally, a single server is enough. But having a single cell battery powering a huge mechanism will only last a century, and there is no safety net in case of malfunction. It is also important to keep threats from monopolizing territories and getting even stronger.
Spam: SNARL…
Player: Speaking of the devil
Odysseus: Brace for another wave!
